===Noun===
{{en-noun|ménages à trois|head=ménage à trois}}

# A [[household]] or [[relationship]] whereby three people live together as [[lover]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1856|author=w:Richard F. Burton|title=First Footsteps in East Africa|publisher=Könemann|year_published=2000|page=105
|passage=Old men frequently marry young girls, but then the portion is high and the '''''ménage à trois''''' common.}}
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|chapter=1|passage="We are certainly going to be happy—we three—in this innocent '''''ménage à trois'''''," she said. "I don't know what more you two men could ask for—or I, either—or the children or Eileen.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1920|title=Lucinda|author=w:Anthony Hope|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/51642/pg51642-images.html|passage={{...}}if she frowned—and there could be no doubt that she was frowning now—what lay before him, before them? A scamped and mean '''''ménage à trois''''', existence eked out with the aid of Mrs. Knyvett’s scanty resources, and soured by her laments!}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2001|author=Sheila Isenberg|title=A Hero of Our Own|page=134
|passage=For a while, he lived in a '''ménage à trois''' with the poet Paul Eluard and his wife, Gala Diakonova (who would later marry Salvador Dali).}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2006|author=Gene Lees|title=Portrait of Johnny|page=56
|passage=I'm not a prude and I wasn't a prude then, but I couldn't see living in a '''''ménage à trois''''' unless the third member were a girl.}}
# {{lb|en|sex}} A sexual act or experience involving three people; a [[threesome]].
#* '''1996''', {{w|Cyrinda Foxe}}, in McNeil & McCain, ''Please Kill Me: The Uncensored Oral History of Punk'', page 134:
#*: David and Angela and I had a '''ménage à trois''' for about five minutes, but then I made her leave because David and I were gonna play.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=November 15 1999|author=John Cloud|title=Henry & Mary & Janet &…|work=Time|passage=No, the two guys don't go for each other; the triad tried a '''ménage à trois''' once but stopped because Chris thought it was icky.}}

